{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781520112,"nonce":"hj/gyvVTdbkIL6/3rGBlIW1k68U=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABFgPM8Q","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/276","origin":"github"},"title":"nav config: re-enable s57 + add bathymetry override layer (supersede #263 interim disable)","message":"Part of #86 (Phase-4 enablement). This is the **nav-config forward fix** that\nsupersedes the field interim, restoring proper global planning at no-ENC inland\nsites once the bathymetry costmap layer exists.\n\n## Background — why planning is degraded now\nAt Lake Massabesic (inland, **no ENC coverage**) the S57 chart layer is empty, so\nthe field-imported interim (#263) **disabled `chart_layer` wholesale** in the local\n+ global costmaps and coarsened the local costmap. That keeps the planner running\nagainst mostly-unknown space (`allow_unknown: true` + rolling window), but it's a\nband-aid: with the chart source gone there's no global depth/obstacle structure, so\nplanning is effectively confined to the local costmap window.\n\n## Forward fix (gated on the bathy layer, #164)\n1. **Add the `bathymetry_layer`** (#164, store-backed clearance) to the local +\n   global costmaps, **ordered AFTER `s57_layer`** so surveyed/contour bathy overrides\n   chart bathy.\n2. **Re-enable `s57_layer`** (revert #263's wholesale disable). At Massabesic it's\n   empty and harmless; at ENC sites it carries charted obstacles while the bathy\n   layer overrides depth. This keeps the config correct everywhere, not lake-only.\n3. **Footgun mitigation:** bathy after s57 must not clear legit non-bathy charted\n   obstacles (docks/wrecks). Interim guard = GeoTIFF lake-outline masking on the\n   bathy layer; the durable fix is the S57 chart-bathy/obstacle split (#14).\n4. **Re-evaluate `allow_unknown` + global rolling window** now that a global depth\n   source exists — global planning should no longer depend on unknown-space traversal.\n\n## Coordination / scope\n- Config lives in the bizzy nav overlay (`nav2_overlay.yaml`, where #263 landed) and\n  the base params; coordinate with the bizzy nav2 override structure (#96).\n- #164 registers the plugin in `nav2_params`; this issue owns **undoing the interim\n  chart disable + the layer ordering + the allow_unknown/window re-evaluation** and\n  verifying global planning is actually restored (sim harness: rolker/unh_marine_simulation#67/#74).\n- Until #164 + the store importer (#148) land, the #263 interim stays in force.\n\n## Acceptance\n- s57 re-enabled; `bathymetry_layer` ordered after it on both costmaps.\n- In the Massabesic sim, the global planner routes across the lake against the\n  bathy prior (not just the local window); shoals are avoided.\n- No regression at an ENC-covered site: charted non-bathy obstacles remain lethal\n  even where surveyed water under them is deep.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}